.el .ds Aq '
.TH gpuq 1  "gpuq 0.3.1" 
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH NAME
gpuq \- GPU scheduler for Linux
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBgpuq\fR [\fB\-\-api\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fB\-V\fR|\fB\-\-version\fR] <\fIsubcommands\fR>
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH DESCRIPTION
GPU scheduler for Linux. Programs request a GPU through gpuq, which grants it by priority class and available VRAM. To free a card, gpuq can signal running jobs, stop and start services, and unload models from LLM servers.
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-api\fR \fI<HOST:PORT>\fR
Address of the gpuq control API (default: $GPUQ_API, else 127.0.0.1:9390)
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.TP
\fB\-V\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
Print version
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
gpuq\-daemon(1)
Run the daemon
.TP
gpuq\-check\-config(1)
Load and validate the config, then exit
.TP
gpuq\-status(1)
Show the arbiter state, leases and queue
.TP
gpuq\-run(1)
Run a command under a GPU lease
.TP
gpuq\-hold(1)
Hold a lease until Ctrl\-C
.TP
gpuq\-desktop(1)
Show or change what gpuq does with the desktop ([desktop] in the config)
.TP
gpuq\-help(1)
Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)
.SH FILES
.TP
\fI/etc/gpuq/config.toml\fR
System configuration.
.TP
\fI~/.config/gpuq/config.toml\fR
User configuration, read when the system one does not exist.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
\fBGPUQ_API\fR
Address of the control API used by the client commands. Default: 127.0.0.1:9390.
.TP
\fBGPUQ_LOG\fR
Log filter for the daemon, for example \fBdebug\fR. \fBRUST_LOG\fR is read when it is unset.
.PP
Commands started by \fBgpuq run\fR receive \fBGPUQ_LEASE_ID\fR, \fBGPUQ_YIELD_FILE\fR
and \fBGPUQ_CARD\fR, the card they got.
.SH EXIT STATUS
The client commands exit with 69 when the daemon does not answer.
.SH SEE ALSO
Configuration reference and integration guides: https://github.com/elektricM/gpuq
